WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.842 --> 00:00:06.346
In this lesson, we do a skin analysis and consultation for a new client,

00:00:06.296 --> 00:00:07.150
step by step.

00:00:07.657 --> 00:00:09.390
Keep these things in mind throughout:

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:14.110
ask before you work, analyze clean skin in good light, and don't diagnose.

00:00:14.751 --> 00:00:15.554
Step one:

00:00:15.862 --> 00:00:16.914
welcome the client.

00:00:17.229 --> 00:00:20.914
Greet her, invite her to sit down, and offer a glass of water.

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:24.834
Invite her to change into a gown, somewhere discreet and private.

00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:28.801
If she wears contact lenses, ask her to take them out first,

00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:31.314
because the magnifying lamp is very bright,

00:00:31.506 --> 00:00:33.474
and you may need to cleanse around the eyes.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:38.034
Then put on a soft fabric headband, to keep the hair away from the face.

00:00:38.186 --> 00:00:41.910
Before touching the client, wash your hands with soap and dry them,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.554
as in the hand hygiene lesson.

00:00:44.229 --> 00:00:45.000
Step two:

00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:46.600
the consultation form.

00:00:47.021 --> 00:00:49.960
Sit at the client's eye level, and ask calmly.

00:00:50.347 --> 00:00:53.320
Allergies, and past reactions to cosmetics.

00:00:53.491 --> 00:00:54.600
Current medication.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:58.520
Products she uses at home, especially retinoids or acids.

00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:00.760
Whether she is taking isotretinoin.

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:03.400
Recent treatments, and sun exposure.

00:01:03.826 --> 00:01:08.200
If she is pregnant, ask more, and choose products as the brand instructs.

00:01:08.462 --> 00:01:09.240
Ask too:

00:01:09.424 --> 00:01:12.840
what does she hope for, and where does her skin feel uncomfortable?

00:01:13.257 --> 00:01:16.680
Ask regular clients again too, because things may have changed.

00:01:16.949 --> 00:01:18.600
And explain why you are asking:

00:01:18.873 --> 00:01:21.640
to choose the right products, and to avoid risks.

00:01:22.044 --> 00:01:24.920
When the client understands, she will answer honestly.

00:01:25.559 --> 00:01:30.310
If anything worries you, like sunburn, a scratch, a cold sore,

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:32.358
or an area that is swollen,

00:01:32.387 --> 00:01:35.318
red and painful, don't work on that area.

00:01:35.771 --> 00:01:40.090
Speak gently, describe what you see, and suggest the client ask a doctor,

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.838
as in the lesson on when not to treat a client.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.364
Step three:

00:01:44.545 --> 00:01:46.604
cleanse, to see the real skin.

00:01:47.111 --> 00:01:50.864
The client lies on the bed, covered with a towel and a blanket,

00:01:50.814 --> 00:01:53.804
leaving only the face, neck and shoulders exposed.

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:58.444
Remove eye and lip makeup very gently, then cleanse the face.

00:01:59.031 --> 00:02:01.804
You will learn cleansing in detail in the basic facial lesson.

00:02:02.384 --> 00:02:06.844
Analyzing skin that still has makeup or cream on it means reading it wrong from the start.

00:02:07.475 --> 00:02:08.376
Step four:

00:02:08.637 --> 00:02:10.936
analysis under the magnifying lamp.

00:02:11.361 --> 00:02:15.336
Place cotton pads over the eyes first, because the lamp is very bright.

00:02:15.898 --> 00:02:19.526
Bring the lamp close, and go through the face area by area,

00:02:19.476 --> 00:02:22.376
always in the same order, so nothing is missed.

00:02:22.948 --> 00:02:23.740
The forehead:

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.100
look at oil, pores, and horizontal lines.

00:02:27.592 --> 00:02:31.260
The T zone, the center of the forehead, the nose and the chin:

00:02:31.614 --> 00:02:34.620
usually the oiliest area, with the most blackheads.

00:02:34.865 --> 00:02:35.660
The cheeks:

00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:40.460
look for redness, small blood vessels, brown spots, and dryness.

00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:42.060
The jawline and chin:

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:45.100
often small spots, and bumps under the skin.

00:02:45.499 --> 00:02:46.860
Finally, the neck:

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:50.460
the skin there is thin, and needs the same care as the face.

00:02:51.123 --> 00:02:52.146
A useful tip:

00:02:52.414 --> 00:02:54.546
look at the skin from several angles.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:03:00.163
Tilt the lamp so the light skims across the skin, and you will clearly see texture,

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:00.546
pores,

00:03:00.656 --> 00:03:01.826
and fine lines.

00:03:02.184 --> 00:03:04.386
Looking straight on, you see color:

00:03:04.641 --> 00:03:07.666
redness, brown spots, dark marks.

00:03:08.015 --> 00:03:11.906
And do not forget around the ears, the hairline, and under the chin.

00:03:12.335 --> 00:03:16.226
Those are places where small spots often appear, and few people notice.

00:03:16.843 --> 00:03:18.469
Here is what you will often see.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.589
Oil in the T zone, while the cheeks are dry:

00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:22.789
combination skin.

00:03:23.286 --> 00:03:25.189
Blackheads on the nose and chin:

00:03:25.348 --> 00:03:26.469
congested skin.

00:03:26.888 --> 00:03:30.309
Redness on the cheeks, with small visible blood vessels:

00:03:30.602 --> 00:03:33.909
the skin is sensitive right now, so work very gently.

00:03:34.249 --> 00:03:36.069
Brown spots on the cheekbones:

00:03:36.172 --> 00:03:38.629
pigmentation, closely linked to the sun.

00:03:39.283 --> 00:03:40.168
Step five:

00:03:40.479 --> 00:03:41.288
the touch test.

00:03:41.686 --> 00:03:45.128
Clean hands, or gloves, following your salon's rules.

00:03:45.533 --> 00:03:49.688
Press a blotting paper gently onto the forehead, nose and cheeks.

00:03:50.035 --> 00:03:52.968
Where the paper turns translucent, there is more oil.

00:03:53.338 --> 00:03:57.208
The test is only accurate once the skin has rested for a while after cleansing.

00:03:57.693 --> 00:04:00.488
Then glide your fingertips lightly over the cheeks:

00:04:00.916 --> 00:04:03.608
is the skin smooth, rough, or tight?

00:04:03.871 --> 00:04:07.128
Any spot that turns pink as soon as you touch it, note it down:

00:04:07.317 --> 00:04:10.088
sensitive skin, so choose gentle products.

00:04:10.772 --> 00:04:11.705
Step six:

00:04:11.811 --> 00:04:12.665
write it down.

00:04:12.928 --> 00:04:16.720
The skin type, the condition of each area, what the client told you,

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.425
and what you decided not to do,

00:04:18.531 --> 00:04:19.225
and why.

00:04:19.635 --> 00:04:22.185
Write what you see, not the name of a disease.

00:04:22.611 --> 00:04:26.505
If you want to photograph the skin to compare next time, ask the client first.

00:04:26.773 --> 00:04:30.505
You can keep this in VaraaAi, in the internal notes on the client record.

00:04:30.754 --> 00:04:34.425
Only the salon can see them, and only write them if the client agrees.

00:04:35.092 --> 00:04:35.871
Step seven:

00:04:36.258 --> 00:04:38.751
choose the treatment, and explain it to the client.

00:04:39.097 --> 00:04:39.871
For example:

00:04:40.097 --> 00:04:44.511
combination skin, slightly dehydrated, a few blackheads on the nose.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:45.471
Then:

00:04:45.574 --> 00:04:49.824
a gentle cleanse, a light exfoliation, a mask that suits the skin,

00:04:49.774 --> 00:04:52.751
and extractions only if you have been trained,

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:54.031
and the salon allows it.

00:04:54.461 --> 00:04:57.134
Tell the client what you will do, how it will feel,

00:04:57.084 --> 00:04:58.831
and what the real result will be.

00:04:59.086 --> 00:05:03.701
If there is something you can't do today, like an area that is red and stinging,

00:05:03.651 --> 00:05:05.071
tell the client clearly,

00:05:05.172 --> 00:05:07.871
and suggest a gentler treatment, or another appointment.

00:05:08.464 --> 00:05:09.314
Step eight:

00:05:09.481 --> 00:05:11.634
home care, and the next appointment.

00:05:11.923 --> 00:05:13.474
Give the client a short plan:

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:18.097
a gentle cleanse morning and evening, a moisturizer that suits her skin type,

00:05:18.047 --> 00:05:19.634
and sunscreen every morning.

00:05:20.143 --> 00:05:22.754
Write it down for her to take home, so she doesn't forget.

00:05:23.103 --> 00:05:23.794
And tell her:

00:05:24.062 --> 00:05:27.613
if her skin feels uncomfortable with a new product, stop using it,

00:05:27.563 --> 00:05:28.834
and let the salon know.

00:05:29.076 --> 00:05:31.557
Then book the next appointment right at the desk,

00:05:31.507 --> 00:05:33.394
to see together how the skin changes.

00:05:34.038 --> 00:05:35.321
After the client leaves:

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:40.419
change the towels and the bed linen, wipe down the bed and the magnifying lamp,

00:05:40.369 --> 00:05:41.721
then wash your hands.

00:05:42.134 --> 00:05:45.081
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
